window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-24c62848a3326493"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"manage-app-updates\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"_1\">管理应用更新</h1> <blockquote> <p>如需完整的文档索引，请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档页面 URL 后添加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取该页面的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p>ChatGPT 桌面应用通常会自行检查并安装更新。如果你的组织需要在用户收到新版本之前进行审查，可以关闭应用内置的更新程序，再通过设备管理平台部署已批准的版本。</p> <p>应用更新程序默认保持启用。将其关闭并不会阻止 Microsoft Store、Microsoft Intune、移动设备管理（MDM）、包管理器或其他外部部署工具安装更新。</p> <p><a id=\"before-you-begin\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">开始之前</h2> <p>请确认你具备以下条件：</p> <ul> <li>对工作区的<a href=\"https://chatgpt.com/codex/settings/managed-configs\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">托管配置（需联网）</a>拥有 Codex 管理员访问权限。</li> <li>一个支持由组织管理更新的 macOS 或 Windows 版 ChatGPT 桌面应用版本。</li> <li>可以在受管理设备上安装已批准应用安装包的 MDM 或软件部署平台。</li> <li>用于测试新版本、部署安全更新和跟踪已安装应用版本的流程。</li> </ul> <p>如果你还没有在 Windows 上部署应用，请先阅读<a href=\"#/article/a-3a9100c321640450\">部署 Windows 应用</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"turn-off-in-app-updates\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">关闭应用内更新</h2> <p>关闭应用内更新后，你的组织有责任及时部署新的应用版本和安全修复。延迟更新可能会让应用及其捆绑组件暴露在已知安全漏洞下。旧版本不会单独获得安全补丁或延长支持。</p> <p>创建一条托管策略，禁用桌面应用自己的更新程序：</p> <ol> <li>打开<a href=\"https://chatgpt.com/codex/settings/managed-configs\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">托管配置（需联网）</a>。</li> <li>选择 <strong>Add policy</strong>；或者打开一条现有策略，用于你要管理的用户、群组或平台。</li> <li>在 <strong>Targets</strong> 下选择 <strong>Add target</strong>，把策略分配给指定的 <strong>Groups</strong>、<strong>Users</strong> 或 <strong>Platforms</strong>。条件允许时，先从一小组试点用户开始。</li> <li>打开 <strong>Raw TOML</strong>，找到 <strong>requirements.toml</strong> 编辑器。</li> <li>添加以下策略：</li> </ol> <pre><code class=\"language-toml\">   [features]\n   in_app_updates = false\n</code></pre> <p>如果策略已经包含 <code>[features]</code> 表，请把 <code>in_app_updates = false</code> 添加到该表中。不要再添加第二个 <code>[features]</code> 表，也不要把此设置放进 <strong>config.toml</strong>。</p> <ol> <li>选择 <strong>Save changes</strong>。</li> <li>请受影响的用户完全退出并重新打开 ChatGPT 桌面应用。仅关闭应用窗口并不一定会重启应用。</li> </ol> <p>有些工作区显示的是策略列表编辑器，而不是 <strong>Raw TOML</strong> 选项卡。在该界面中，请直接把同一个 TOML 块添加到相应策略中；如果可以，请使用 <strong>Groups</strong> 分配策略，然后选择 <strong>Save</strong>。</p> <p>有关托管策略传递和优先级的详情，请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-77481efb12a63f4e\">托管配置</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"verify-the-managed-setting\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">验证托管设置</h2> <p>应用重新启动后，请在一名受影响用户的设备上验证策略：</p> <ol> <li>使用策略覆盖的账号登录 ChatGPT 桌面应用。</li> <li>打开 <strong>Settings</strong> &gt; <strong>General</strong>。</li> <li>找到 <strong>In-app updates</strong>，确认它显示 <strong>Managed</strong>，并显示消息“Your organization has turned off in-app updates.”（你的组织已关闭应用内更新）。</li> <li>确认设备管理平台仍然可以部署已批准的应用版本。</li> </ol> <p>即使策略阻止应用内更新，<strong>Check for Updates</strong> 菜单项也可能继续显示。请通过 <strong>Managed</strong> 指示器验证策略，而不是根据该菜单项是否出现来判断。</p> <p>如果第一次重启后没有出现该指示器，应用可能仍在使用缓存的策略。请等待策略刷新，然后再次完全退出并重新打开应用。在 <strong>Managed</strong> 出现之前，不要依赖这项更新限制。</p> <p><a id=\"deploy-approved-app-versions\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_5\">部署已批准的应用版本</h2> <p>关闭应用内更新后，请使用现有设备管理流程发布新版本：</p> <ol> <li>选择组织准备部署的应用版本。</li> <li>为设备群中的每种操作系统和设备架构获取受支持的安装包。</li> <li>使用一小组具有代表性的用户测试该版本。</li> <li>通过 Microsoft Intune、MDM 平台或其他软件部署工具发布已批准的安装包。</li> <li>检查设备清单，确认平台安装了预期版本，然后把发布范围扩大到其他群组。</li> </ol> <p>如何分阶段发布、选择版本，以及部署没有完成时如何恢复，都由你的管理平台决定。如果平台允许回滚，恢复到旧版本并不会延长支持，也不能保证服务兼容性。</p> <p>对于 macOS，请下载 <a href=\"https://persistent.oaistatic.com/codex-app-prod/ChatGPT.dmg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">ChatGPT 桌面应用安装程序（需联网）</a>。有关 Windows 安装方法和针对不同架构的安装包，请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-3a9100c321640450\">部署 Windows 应用</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"turn-in-app-updates-back-on\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_6\">重新打开应用内更新</h2> <p>要恢复应用的正常更新行为：</p> <ol> <li>找出所有会为受影响用户关闭更新的托管策略、系统 <code>requirements.toml</code> 文件和 MDM 配置文件。</li> <li>从每个适用的 <code>[features]</code> 表中删除 <code>in_app_updates = false</code>。</li> <li>保存策略更改，并重新部署所有已更新、由设备管理的 requirements 配置。</li> <li>请受影响的用户完全退出并重新打开 ChatGPT 桌面应用。</li> <li>检查 <strong>Settings</strong> &gt; <strong>General</strong>，确认由托管策略控制的 <strong>In-app updates</strong> 行不再出现。</li> </ol> <p>当没有任何适用策略设置 <code>in_app_updates = false</code> 时，应用的内置更新程序会恢复正常行为。如果 <strong>Managed</strong> 指示器仍然存在，请检查其他工作区策略、MDM 配置文件和系统 <code>requirements.toml</code> 文件。各托管来源的应用顺序请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-77481efb12a63f4e?anchor=locations-and-precedence\">位置和优先级</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"understand-security-and-support-responsibilities\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_7\">了解安全与支持责任</h2> <p>应用接收并应用托管更新策略后，该策略会：</p> <ul> <li>阻止桌面应用通过自身的更新程序检查、下载或安装更新。</li> <li>不会提供由 OpenAI 管理的版本固定、独立发布通道，也不保证旧版本的服务兼容性。</li> <li>应用于受支持 macOS 和 Windows 构建上的 ChatGPT 桌面应用；不会管理移动应用、Codex CLI 或 IDE 扩展的更新。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"troubleshoot-common-issues\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_8\">排查常见问题</h2> <p>如果身份验证问题、连接问题或超时导致应用无法获取或应用托管策略，其内置更新程序可能会继续启用。在 <strong>Managed</strong> 出现之前，不要假定应用已经阻止更新。</p> <p>如果没有出现 <strong>Managed</strong> 指示器，请确认：</p> <ul> <li>受影响用户选择了预期工作区。</li> <li>策略以该用户、群组或平台为目标。</li> <li>设备运行受支持的应用版本。</li> <li>应用可以连接到传递托管策略的服务。</li> <li>设置位于 <strong>requirements.toml</strong>，而不是 <strong>config.toml</strong>。</li> <li>保存策略后，用户已完全退出并重新打开应用。</li> </ul> <p>如果无法打开托管配置或保存策略，请确认你对该工作区拥有 Codex 管理员访问权限。</p> <p>如果关闭应用内更新后，应用版本仍发生变化，请检查是否由 Microsoft Store、Intune、MDM、包管理器或其他部署系统安装了更新。该策略只控制应用自己的内置更新程序。</p> <p><a id=\"related-docs\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_9\">相关文档</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-77481efb12a63f4e\">托管配置</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-3a9100c321640450\">部署 Windows 应用</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-c2332644faa13713?anchor=requirementstoml\"><code>requirements.toml</code> 配置参考</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-811aa7aeaf6b8cd4\">管理员发布指南</a></li> </ul>","en":"<h1 id=\"manage-app-updates\">Manage app updates</h1> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <p>The ChatGPT desktop app normally checks for and installs updates on its own. If your organization needs to review new releases before users receive them, you can turn off the app's built-in updater and deploy approved versions through your device management platform.</p> <p>The app's updater remains enabled by default. Turning it off doesn't stop Microsoft Store, Microsoft Intune, mobile device management (MDM), package managers, or other external deployment tools from installing updates.</p> <h2 id=\"before-you-begin\">Before you begin</h2> <p>Confirm that you have:</p> <ul> <li>Codex administrator access to <a href=\"https://chatgpt.com/codex/settings/managed-configs\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Managed configuration (online)</a> for your workspace.</li> <li>A ChatGPT desktop app release for macOS or Windows that supports organization-managed updates.</li> <li>An MDM or software-deployment platform that can install approved app packages on your managed devices.</li> <li>A process for testing new releases, deploying security updates, and tracking installed app versions.</li> </ul> <p>If you haven't deployed the app on Windows, start with <a href=\"#/article/a-3a9100c321640450\">Deploy the Windows app</a>.</p> <h2 id=\"turn-off-in-app-updates\">Turn off in-app updates</h2> <p>When you turn off in-app updates, your organization is responsible for promptly deploying new app releases and security fixes. Delaying updates can leave the app and its bundled components exposed to known security vulnerabilities. Older app versions don't receive separate security patches or extended support.</p> <p>Create a managed policy that disables the desktop app's own updater:</p> <ol> <li>Open <a href=\"https://chatgpt.com/codex/settings/managed-configs\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Managed configuration (online)</a>.</li> <li>Select <strong>Add policy</strong>, or open an existing policy for the users, groups, or platforms you want to manage.</li> <li>Under <strong>Targets</strong>, select <strong>Add target</strong> to assign the policy to specific <strong>Groups</strong>, <strong>Users</strong>, or <strong>Platforms</strong>. Start with a small pilot group when possible.</li> <li>Open <strong>Raw TOML</strong> and find the <strong>requirements.toml</strong> editor.</li> <li>Add the following policy:</li> </ol> <pre><code class=\"language-toml\">   [features]\n   in_app_updates = false\n</code></pre> <p>If your policy already contains a <code>[features]</code> table, add <code>in_app_updates = false</code> to that table. Don't add a second <code>[features]</code> table or put the setting in <strong>config.toml</strong>.</p> <ol> <li>Select <strong>Save changes</strong>.</li> <li>Ask affected users to fully quit and reopen the ChatGPT desktop app. Closing the app window isn't always enough to restart the application.</li> </ol> <p>Some workspaces show a policy-list editor instead of the <strong>Raw TOML</strong> tab. In that interface, add the same TOML block directly to the applicable policy, use <strong>Groups</strong> to assign it when available, and select <strong>Save</strong>.</p> <p>For details about managed policy delivery and precedence, see <a href=\"#/article/a-77481efb12a63f4e\">Managed configuration</a>.</p> <h2 id=\"verify-the-managed-setting\">Verify the managed setting</h2> <p>After the app restarts, verify the policy from an affected user's device:</p> <ol> <li>Sign in to the ChatGPT desktop app with an account covered by the policy.</li> <li>Open <strong>Settings</strong> &gt; <strong>General</strong>.</li> <li>Find <strong>In-app updates</strong> and confirm that it shows <strong>Managed</strong> and the message “Your organization has turned off in-app updates.”</li> <li>Confirm that your device management platform can still deploy an approved app version.</li> </ol> <p>The <strong>Check for Updates</strong> menu option can remain visible even when the policy blocks in-app updates. Use the <strong>Managed</strong> indicator to verify the policy instead of checking whether that menu option appears.</p> <p>If the indicator doesn't appear after the first restart, the app might still use a cached policy. Allow the policy to refresh, then fully quit and reopen the app again. Don't rely on the update restriction until <strong>Managed</strong> appears.</p> <h2 id=\"deploy-approved-app-versions\">Deploy approved app versions</h2> <p>After you turn off in-app updates, use your existing device management process to deliver new releases:</p> <ol> <li>Choose an app version that your organization plans to deploy.</li> <li>Get the supported installation package for each operating system and device architecture in your fleet.</li> <li>Test the release with a small group of representative users.</li> <li>Deploy the approved package through Microsoft Intune, your MDM platform, or another software-deployment tool.</li> <li>Check device inventory to confirm your platform installed the intended version, then expand the rollout to other groups.</li> </ol> <p>Your management platform determines how you stage releases, select versions, and recover when a deployment doesn't complete. If your platform permits rollback, returning to an older version doesn't extend support or guarantee service compatibility.</p> <p>For macOS, download the <a href=\"https://persistent.oaistatic.com/codex-app-prod/ChatGPT.dmg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">ChatGPT desktop app installer (online)</a>. For Windows installation methods and architecture-specific packages, see <a href=\"#/article/a-3a9100c321640450\">Deploy the Windows app</a>.</p> <h2 id=\"turn-in-app-updates-back-on\">Turn in-app updates back on</h2> <p>To restore the app's normal update behavior:</p> <ol> <li>Identify the managed policies, system <code>requirements.toml</code> files, and MDM profiles that turn off updates for the affected users.</li> <li>Remove <code>in_app_updates = false</code> from each applicable <code>[features]</code> table.</li> <li>Save the policy changes and redeploy any updated device-managed requirements.</li> <li>Ask affected users to fully quit and reopen the ChatGPT desktop app.</li> <li>Check <strong>Settings</strong> &gt; <strong>General</strong> to confirm that the <strong>In-app updates</strong> managed row no longer appears.</li> </ol> <p>When no applicable policy sets <code>in_app_updates = false</code>, the app's built-in updater follows its normal behavior. If the <strong>Managed</strong> indicator still appears, review other workspace policies, MDM profiles, and system <code>requirements.toml</code> files. See <a href=\"#/article/a-77481efb12a63f4e?anchor=locations-and-precedence\">Locations and precedence</a> for the order in which managed sources apply.</p> <h2 id=\"understand-security-and-support-responsibilities\">Understand security and support responsibilities</h2> <p>After the app receives and applies it, the managed update policy:</p> <ul> <li>Prevents the desktop app from checking for, downloading, or installing updates through its own updater.</li> <li>Doesn't provide OpenAI-managed version pinning, a separate release channel, or guaranteed service compatibility for older versions.</li> <li>Applies to the ChatGPT desktop app on supported macOS and Windows builds. It doesn't manage updates for mobile apps, Codex CLI, or the IDE extension.</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"troubleshoot-common-issues\">Troubleshoot common issues</h2> <p>If an authentication problem, connection issue, or timeout prevents the app from retrieving or applying the managed policy, its built-in updater can remain enabled. Don't assume the app blocks updates unless <strong>Managed</strong> appears.</p> <p>If the <strong>Managed</strong> indicator doesn't appear, confirm that:</p> <ul> <li>The affected user selected the intended workspace.</li> <li>The policy targets that user, group, or platform.</li> <li>The device runs a supported app version.</li> <li>The app can connect to the service that delivers managed policies.</li> <li>The setting is in <strong>requirements.toml</strong>, not <strong>config.toml</strong>.</li> <li>The user fully quit and reopened the app after you saved the policy.</li> </ul> <p>If you can't open Managed configuration or save a policy, confirm that you have Codex administrator access for the workspace.</p> <p>If the app version changes after you disable in-app updates, check whether Microsoft Store, Intune, MDM, a package manager, or another deployment system installed the update. The policy controls only the app's built-in updater.</p> <h2 id=\"related-docs\">Related docs</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-77481efb12a63f4e\">Managed configuration</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-3a9100c321640450\">Deploy the Windows app</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-c2332644faa13713?anchor=requirementstoml\"><code>requirements.toml</code> configuration reference</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-811aa7aeaf6b8cd4\">Admin rollout guide</a></li> </ul>"};
